From fc55cb4db23a15f6c4e1ed11be15b9b9b1020dec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tokenjunkielabs <tokenjunkielabs@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:14:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat: add selectFromDb hook to custom types (all
 dialects)

Adds an optional selectFromDb mapper to customType params so a custom
column can transform the SQL emitted when it is read from the database
(SELECT field lists, RETURNING clauses, and relational query JSON
payloads) while fromDriver/toDriver mapping stays unchanged.

- Column gains an optional selectFromDb member; mapColumnSelection()
  applies it to the column's reference SQL
- All five dialects (pg, mysql, sqlite, singlestore, gel) wrap selected
  custom columns and alias the expression back to the column name
- Selections through a materialized subquery/CTE skip the hook so the
  transform is not applied twice to already-transformed output
- Nested relational JSON payloads wrap the column reference exactly once
- SQLite keeps the NumericBigInt text cast inside the read expression
- New tests cover plain/joined selects, returning clauses, subquery and
  CTE reads, relational findMany and nested `with` payloads, and all
  five dialect code paths

Refs: drizzle-team/drizzle-orm#1083, drizzle-team/drizzle-orm#554
